# The opening of the game: the title over the dark sea, then (on a new
# voyage) the night the lantern pulled you from it. Played by the Opening
# node in scenes/prototype/sea.tscn. Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# A cutscene is a conversation whose @ cues stage the scene. Lines wait for
# the Interact button; cues that take time (a fade, a wait, a clip) hold the
# script until they're done. Every cue is listed in
# scripts/cutscene/cue_list.gd.
#
# Where things are, so you can change them without touching this file:
# - Shots (where the camera goes) and marks (where people stand) are
#   Marker3D nodes. The bunk room's are in scenes/prototype/ship.tscn under
#   Shots and Marks; the rescue's are in scenes/prototype/intro/rescue_set.tscn.
# - Clips (@play, @start) are animations. The underwater ones are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/underwater.tscn: open it, select Clips, and the
#   timeline at the bottom of the editor shows them. Each moves the set's
#   camera too, so a clip is also a shot.
# - Sounds (@sound) are the players under SoundCues in sea.tscn. Some have
#   no recording yet (plunge, bell, flare, deep_note, gasp):
#   they're silent until one is put where the player's Recording points.
# - The title is her nameboard at the stern: the letters, the hook, the
#   lantern on it and his clips (takes_watch, hears, dives, welcome) are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/stern_watch.tscn.
# - His looks (@look) are listed in scripts/companion/lantern_face.gd.
#
# To tune one beat: set Start Section on the Opening node to its name and
# the game opens there. While it runs, F8 reads this file again and replays
# the section you're in.

# Her name. The lantern on his hook at the stern, swinging, lights the
# carved board a few letters at a time. It waits for any button. With a
# saved voyage it asks whether to carry it on or start a new one; a new one
# asks who you are, then he hears something.
~ start
@hide heron
@play takes_watch
@look hook_lantern tired
@shot the_board cut
@fade in 3.0
@wait_for any Press any button
@sound confirm
? saved_voyage
-> voyage_menu
-> who_are_you

# With a saved voyage: carry it on, or start again. A new voyage leaves the
# old save until you next sleep in your bunk, which replaces it.
~ voyage_menu
- Continue your voyage -> carry_on
- Start a new voyage -> who_are_you

# A saved voyage: he turns from her name to the lit windows, pleased to see
# you. Then to black, and the Opening loads the voyage and shows which day it is.
~ carry_on
@continue_voyage
@look hook_lantern pleased
@play welcome
@wait 0.8
@show heron
@fade out 0.8
@play off_watch
@shot free cut

# A new voyage: who are you, a boy or a girl? Asked over her name, and it
# waits for the answer.
~ who_are_you
@who_are_you
-> the_stern

# The Prologue's first scene (docs/prologue.md, #182). A quiet night
# first. Then he's seen something: faint lights, far down in the water. The
# swinging stops and the camera draws back from her name to the stern, the
# black sea and the rain, and the captain at the wheel above. He leans out
# on his hook and calls up to him. (The shots are markers in
# scenes/prototype/intro/stern_watch.tscn: TheBoard, TheStern, TheHook and
# TheWheel. The captain stands on its Wheel mark.)
~ the_stern
@play takes_watch
@shot the_board cut
@look hook_lantern tired
@place heron wheel
@show heron
@wait 1.6
@look hook_lantern surprised
@play hears
@grave on
@shot the_stern
@wait 1.2
@look hook_lantern pleased
lantern: There you are...
@play looks_out
lantern: I knew I hadn't imagined it.
lantern: Captain? I think I've found something.
@shot the_wheel cut
heron: Something, or another one of your little lights?
@shot the_hook cut
@look hook_lantern determined
lantern: I know the difference!
@shot the_wheel cut
heron: Do you?
@shot the_hook cut
@look hook_lantern calm
lantern: Look.
-> the_grave

# The camera goes past him, out over the water and down: the Grave of the
# Lanterns. Thousands of them, empty, some broken, some caught in great
# chains, a few still glowing like dying stars, and no bottom. (The set is
# scenes/prototype/intro/grave.tscn; its camera moves are the clips
# over_the_grave, that_one, passes_below and finds_the_hand.)
~ the_grave
@stage grave
@play over_the_grave
lantern: There must be hundreds of them.
heron: Thousands, most likely.
lantern: I wonder how long they've been down there.
heron: Longer than either of us.
@play that_one
lantern: Wait. That one...
-> something_down_there

# Back up top. He leans further, and something rings, far below.
~ something_down_there
@stage off
@shot the_hook cut
@look hook_lantern worried
lantern: Captain, I think there's something down there.
@shot the_wheel cut
heron: Don't lean too far over.
@shot the_hook cut
@look hook_lantern determined
lantern: I'm not!
@play leans_further
@sound ring
@wait 1.8
@look hook_lantern surprised
lantern: That's strange.
-> the_shape

# Something moves beneath the ship: far down, something too big to be
# anything passes under them, seen only by what it hides, and the lanterns
# rock in its wake.
~ the_shape
@stage grave
@start steadies
@say_in 2.5 heron 2.6 Back away from the rail.
@say_in 5.6 lantern 2.2 I think I saw—
@play passes_below
-> the_hand

# Something drifting amongst the dead lights. At first it looks like
# another broken lantern. Then: a hand.
~ the_hand
@stage grave
@play finds_the_hand
lantern: ...
lantern: Captain?
heron: What is it?
lantern: There's somebody in the water.
-> overboard

# Back up top. He shouts it, and the captain turns, too late: before he's
# finished, the lantern is off the hook and over the side.
~ overboard
@stage off
@shot the_wheel cut
heron: What?
@shot the_hook cut
@look hook_lantern determined
lantern: Somebody overboard!
@shot the_wheel cut
@face heron hook
@say heron 1.4 Don't you dare—
@wait 0.7
@shot the_hook cut
@start dives
@wait 0.3
-> plunge

# The plunge. From out on the water: the storm sea, the ship's stern, and
# one small point of light arcing out from her through the rain. It hits
# the water, and it's gone.
~ plunge
@look flying_lantern determined
@show flying_lantern
@shot the_plunge cut
@play off_watch
@start flies
@wait 1.45
@sound plunge
@wait 1.5
@hide flying_lantern
-> dark

# The dark. The storm stops dead as the water closes over, and he's
# already in it. Far above, a bell: somebody heard him.
~ dark
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@sound bell
-> light

# The light. A small warm thing comes through the surface, a long way off,
# and drives down through the dark in three hard pushes. Each one costs
# him: he's smaller and colder with each, and reaches you nearly out. His
# weak light finds dim shapes hanging all round: lanterns, like him.
~ light
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern determined
@look sinking_lantern clear
@look sinking_lantern mended
@play lantern_appears
@play lantern_drives
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play lantern_arrives
-> reach

# The reach. A flame can't reach through glass, so he opens his own door,
# and the sea comes in. He tells you what to do. The hand forms and fails,
# and he urges you; it fails again, he looks once at the others hanging
# there, and he asks. After that he says nothing, and holds it out, for as
# long as it takes. You can take it at any moment.
~ reach
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play opens_door
@look sinking_lantern cracked
@look sinking_lantern pleading
@start pleads
@queue offered
@say lantern 2.2 Grab my hand!
@say_in 4.3 lantern 2.2 Come on. Come on.
@say_in 9.1 lantern 2.2 ...Please.
@wait_for interact Take his hand
@sound grasp
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play taken
-> out

# Out. The moment your hands close, your hand catches him alight again:
# everything blooms, your eyes open, and for a moment his light reaches a
# long way down. There's no bottom to see. Hanging below
# you at every depth are more of them, fainter and fainter until the murk
# takes them. Then he turns upward and takes your weight.
~ out
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@start flares
@sound flare
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@wait 5.6
-> haul

# The haul. From above him, down the line of his arm: he drags you up in
# hard pushes, the others falling away beneath you. Lightning lands on his
# pushes and comes down past you in shafts. A very long way down there's
# an outline, and it's moving. He doesn't look. He tells you not to, and
# then there's time to look anyway, in the lightning, with nothing said.
~ haul
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@start hauls
@wait 0.4
@say lantern 1.8 Hold on.
@wait 1.4
@hush on
@sound deep_note
@wait 0.4
@lightning
@wait 2.0
@say lantern 2.2 Don't look down.
@wait 2.6
@lightning
@wait 1.4
@lightning
@wait 1.8
@hush off
-> rising

# The last of it: two more pushes, and the surface.
~ rising
@stage underwater
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play rising
@fade out 0.4
-> surface

# The surface. You burst up into the storm, gasping, his hand still in
# yours. Then the roles flip: he's a small ember with his door hanging open,
# he settles into your hand, and you hold him up out of the waves, the ship
# towering ahead. He's done his part, and his eyes close.
~ surface
@stage off
@muffle off
@show castaway
@look rescued_lantern tired
@shot surfacing cut
@start surfaces
@fade in 0.15
@sound gasp
@wait 2.4
@look rescued_lantern asleep
@wait 1.4
-> rail

# The rail. Lightning shows a tall thin shape up there against the sky,
# looking down at one point of warm light on a black sea: the answer to his
# shout, a minute late. It doesn't move. Then a long fade to black. How you
# got aboard isn't shown: the boathook leaning by the galley door,
# afterwards, says it.
~ rail
@show castaway
@look rescued_lantern asleep
@place heron rail
@show heron
@shot the_rail cut
@wait 0.9
@lightning
@wait 1.8
@fade out 2.5
@hide castaway
@hide heron
@play off_watch
-> asleep

# Black, for a while. Then, slowly, the bunk room at night, the storm
# outside: you asleep in your bunk. He isn't beside you: he's on his round
# table by the stove, small and blue, his glass cracked, and silent. The sea
# took nearly all of him (#158).
~ asleep
@hide heron
@hide player
@show sleeping_you
@home lantern
@look lantern tired
@look lantern cracked
set lantern_low
@shot in_your_bunk cut
@wait 1.5
@fade in 3.0
@wait 0.8
-> waking

# It's the captain who wakes you, from the doorway.
~ waking
heron: Up. You've slept enough for two.
@start wakes
@wait 1.2
-> doorway

# A tall shadow in the doorway: the captain, come to look you over. By the
# time we look back you're up, by your bunk. He's gruff, and not worried,
# he'd tell you; he looks at the lantern anyway.
~ doorway
@hide sleeping_you
@show player
@place heron doorway
@show heron
@face heron player
@shot doorway cut
@wait 0.8
heron: Nobody drowns on my ship. Nobody goes hungry either.
heron: You've managed the first.
@face heron lantern
@shot stove_nook
@wait 1.5
heron: He's not said a word since.
@wait 0.8
@face heron player
@shot doorway
heron: I don't know lamps. I know ships.
heron: You held on to him out there. See if you can't hold on a bit longer.
-> yours

# Then the ship is yours. The captain goes about his business: up on deck
# for a drink at the water butt, and back to his fire (the FirstQuest node
# in sea.tscn walks him there and back).
~ yours
@shot free cut
